From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:51:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: read HEVC slice headers of
 pictures sent without them

Chromium's V4L2 stateless HEVC decoder sends each picture as Annex-B NAL
units in one OUTPUT buffer with the SPS, PPS, scaling matrix and decode
parameters, and no SLICE_PARAMS or entry points. The instruction builder
programs the hardware only from SLICE_PARAMS, so it used whatever an
earlier request left in that control: the decoder never raised its
interrupt, every picture timed out, and the resets that followed made
the storm guard rest the decoder for every client.

Select by what the request carries:

- A request with SLICE_PARAMS (VA-API) takes the present path unchanged.
- A request without them has its slice segment headers read from the
  picture (H.265 7.3.6.1-7.3.6.3) when the new hevc_frame_parse
  parameter is set: reference lists as DPB indices built from the decode
  parameters (8.3.4) with the slice's list modification, chroma offsets
  derived (7-56), the short-term and long-term set parts skipped by the
  sizes the decode parameters give. Each slice's region runs from the
  end of the previous one, so start codes and other NAL units count as
  header bytes and the regions stay contiguous as the builder expects.
- Anything else (no SLICE_PARAMS and the parameter off, or a picture
  that is not Annex-B or cannot be read) is refused before it reaches
  the hardware, with one warning per boot when the parameter is off.

hevc_frame_parse defaults to off and is writable at runtime; the
START_CODE control offers ANNEX_B only in contexts opened while it is
set (its default stays NONE, which is what VA-API reads).

A KUnit suite covers the Annex-B detector, I/P/B headers with list
modification, weights and entry points, the region layout across
3- and 4-byte start codes and a non-slice NAL unit, and refusals.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
